cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "UPWIND"
message: "If you use UPWIND, please cite this release. Review the documented scientific limitations before interpreting results."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Pandya
    given-names: Arnav
    affiliation: Independent project
repository-code: "https://github.com/apandya55/Upwind"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-10-29
abstract: >-
  UPWIND is an AI-assisted research software project and public atlas for
  exploring historical PM2.5 evidence while preserving distinctions between
  point estimates, monitor measurements, and emissions inventory records.
  Its experimental local engine has synthetic evaluation evidence only and
  does not establish field accuracy or source attribution.
keywords:
  - air quality
  - PM2.5
  - environmental data
  - research software
